  "summary": "Six preprints from mid-November 2026 embed spin, charge, Clifford or RG structure into quantum diagonalization, state loading and ground-state search.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is exploiting structure, whether exact symmetry or problem-specific approximation, to reduce resources in quantum and quantum-inspired simulation. Spin-adapted SqDRIFT completes sampled configurations to give exact S^2 eigenstates, and a loading circuit prepares U(1)×SU(2)-symmetric MPS for fault-tolerant algorithms with reduced Toffoli cost. Hybrid Clifford-tensor network DMRG lowers bond dimension up to 40x for 2D Ising models. Sparse quantum prolate diagonalization uses compressed sensing to reduce sample complexity from O(N_s) to O(log N_s), with a trapped-ion molecular demonstration. A strong-disorder-RG-guided variational circuit was run on a 16-qubit IQM device. A block-encoding framework for 2D elastic finite element analysis is the outlier, applying the same efficient-encoding approach outside electronic structure and spin models.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
